---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Scheduling and Duplicating Library Workouts — Chiron Support"
  description="Learn how to schedule a Library workout to your own or an athlete's calendar, and how to duplicate a workout to create a progressive variation."
>
  <section class="py-20">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">

      <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-8">
        <a href="/support-center" class="hover:text-primary-600">Support Center</a>
        <span class="mx-2">›</span>
        <span class="text-gray-700">Scheduling and Duplicating Library Workouts</span>
      </nav>

      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">
        Scheduling and Duplicating Library Workouts
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-12">
        Applies to all workout types.
      </p>

      <!-- Schedule a Library workout -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-8 mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Schedule a Library workout</h2>
        <ol class="space-y-4 text-gray-700 mb-6">
          <li class="flex">
            <span class="font-bold text-primary-600 mr-3">1.</span>
            <span>Navigate to the Workout Library: <strong>Schedule → Add → Library Workout</strong>, or <strong>More → Workout Library</strong>.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex">
            <span class="font-bold text-primary-600 mr-3">2.</span>
            <span>Find the workout and tap <strong>Schedule</strong>.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex">
            <span class="font-bold text-primary-600 mr-3">3.</span>
            <span>Select the date.</span>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-700 mb-6">
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-primary-600 mr-2 mt-1">•</span>
            <span><strong>Athletes</strong> — the workout is added to your own schedule. Tap Confirm.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-primary-600 mr-2 mt-1">•</span>
            <span><strong>Coaches</strong> — select yourself and/or any of your athletes from the list, then tap Confirm. The workout is added to each selected schedule.</span>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <figure class="mt-6">
          <img
            src="/images/support-center/scheduling-and-duplicating-library-workouts/chiron-coach-scheduling-athlete-select.png"
            alt="The scheduling dialog in Chiron showing a coach selecting multiple athletes to receive a Library workout"
            class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 shadow-sm mx-auto max-w-xs"
          />
          <figcaption class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 text-center">Coaches can schedule a workout to multiple athletes at once</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <!-- Duplicate a Library workout -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-8 mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Duplicate a Library workout</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
          Duplicating lets you create a variation — a progressive overload version, for example — without modifying the original.
        </p>
        <ol class="space-y-4 text-gray-700 mb-6">
          <li class="flex">
            <span class="font-bold text-primary-600 mr-3">1.</span>
            <span>In the Workout Library, find the workout.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex">
            <span class="font-bold text-primary-600 mr-3">2.</span>
            <span>Tap the three-dot menu → <strong>Duplicate</strong>.</span>
          </li>
          <li class="flex">
            <span class="font-bold text-primary-600 mr-3">3.</span>
            <span>A copy appears in the Library — tap it to rename and edit.</span>
          </li>
        </ol>

        <figure class="mt-6">
          <img
            src="/images/support-center/scheduling-and-duplicating-library-workouts/chiron-workout-context-menu-duplicate.png"
            alt="The workout context menu in Chiron showing the Duplicate option"
            class="rounded-lg border border-gray-200 shadow-sm mx-auto max-w-xs"
          />
          <figcaption class="text-sm text-gray-500 mt-2 text-center">Tap the three-dot menu to find the Duplicate option</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <!-- Related articles -->
      <div class="bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md p-8 mb-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Related articles</h2>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-700">
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-primary-600 mr-2 mt-1">•</span>
            <a href="/support-center/strength-and-conditioning" class="text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-700 hover:underline">Strength &amp; Conditioning in Chiron</a>
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-start">
            <span class="text-primary-600 mr-2 mt-1">•</span>
            <a href="/support-center/recording-a-strength-workout" class="text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-700 hover:underline">Recording a Strength Workout</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <!-- Back / Contact -->
      <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-8 text-center">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">Need More Help?</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
          Can't find what you're looking for? Get in touch with our team.
        </p>
        <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
          <a
            href="/support-center"
            class="inline-block bg-white border border-primary-600 text-primary-600 px-8 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold hover:bg-primary-50 transition-colors"
          >
            Back to Support Center
          </a>
          <a
            href="/support-center/contact"
            class="inline-block bg-primary-600 text-white px-8 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold hover:bg-primary-700 transition-colors"
          >
            Contact Us
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
